<Ui>
    <!--
        benilla's taxi-map window (decision 0484 phase 2): a faithful port of the real 1.12
        `TaxiFrame.{xml,lua}` (patch chain; scratchpad `ref-TaxiFrame.xml/.lua`, line citations
        inline) onto the taxi engine seam (`crates/benilla-ui/src/script/taxi.rs`) fed by
        `crates/benilla/src/ui_taxi.rs`. The window art/geometry are quoted from the reference
        verbatim (384×512, the four TaxiFrame quadrant slabs at 256/128 split, the 316×352 map
        rect at TOP -13,-75) — the deviations below are all where THIS ENGINE, not taste, draws
        the line, each flagged and reasoned like every other transcribed window (Gossip/Merchant/
        Trainer's own header notes).

        Modeled on MerchantFrame.xml/TrainerFrame.xml for the framing: the NPC-session lifecycle
        (RegisterEvent pair, OPENED/CLOSED dispatch, OnShow/OnHide PlaySound with a client-side
        close on hide), the "npc" model-portrait binding, the minimize-button close X (this engine
        ships no UIPanelCloseButton), and the UIPanel slot system (NO hardcoded `<Anchors>` on the
        root — ShowUIPanel/SetLeftFrame SetPoints it to the left slot on open, exactly like every
        other NPC window).

        DEVIATIONS from the literal reference, each forced by this engine (never taste):

        1. NODE BUTTONS ARE A STATIC POOL, not `CreateFrame(..., "TaxiButtonTemplate")` grown on
           demand (ref l.36-42/TaxiFrame.lua:36-42). This engine's runtime `CreateFrame`'s 4th
           `inherits` argument is explicitly a no-op — template expansion is the XML LOADER's job
           only (`benilla-ui/src/script/object.rs`'s `create_frame`: "inherits/template expansion
           is the XML loader's job — ignored"). Every other list window in this codebase hits the
           identical wall and solves it identically: Gossip's 8-row pool, Trainer's service-row
           pool, QuestLog's row pool — a fixed set of concrete `inherits=` instances (which DOES
           expand at LOAD time), shown/hidden/repositioned per repaint instead of created on
           demand. `BENILLA_TAXI_MAX_NODES = 50` below comfortably covers the real 5875
           `TaxiNodes.dbc`'s per-continent max (43 nodes on Eastern Kingdoms, 39 on Kalimdor —
           counted this session, `crate::ui_taxi`'s module doc). The route-line textures stay
           genuinely dynamic (`TaxiRouteMap:CreateTexture(...)`, ref l.101/142) — plain
           region creation carries no template/inherits, so THAT half of the reference runs
           completely unmodified.
        2. THE TITLE READS AN EVENT ARG, not `UnitName("npc")` (ref TaxiFrame.lua:27). This
           engine's `"npc"` unit token (decision 0421) only feeds the PORTRAIT bake — there is no
           backing `UnitState` for `UnitName` to read from it. Gossip/Merchant/Trainer hit the
           identical gap and all solve it the same way: the app resolves the flight master's name
           through the `NameCache` and rides it in as the open event's arg1 — done here too
           (`BenillaTaxiFrame_SetTitle`, fed by `TAXIMAP_OPENED`'s arg1).
        3. (Retired.) The "no single-hop destination" refusal (`DrawOneHopLines`, ref l.161-164)
           used to call a plain `BenillaErrorsFrame_AddMessage` global because this engine had no
           MessageFrame widget for `UIErrorsFrame` to be. It has one now, so the line below is the
           reference's own `UIErrorsFrame:AddMessage(ERR_TAXINOPATHS, ...)`. `ErrorsFrame.xml` loads
           well before this file in the shipped list (`ui_script/mod.rs`), so the frame already
           exists by the time this ever runs.

        `<TaxiRouteFrame>` (an intrinsic type this engine doesn't have) becomes a plain `<Frame>`
        (`TaxiRouteMap`) per the house rule for every non-shipped intrinsic (decision 0246's
        patch-chain rule; the `Cooldown`/`GameTooltip`/etc. precedents) — it carries no behavior of
        its own beyond being a Frame that owns child regions/buttons, so the plain type loses
        nothing.

        Money (the fare) renders as plain text via `SetTooltipMoney` on the shared `GameTooltip`
        (`GameTooltip.xml`'s own seam) exactly like the reference — no `BenillaMoney_*` coin rig
        needed here (that lives on the merchant/trainer purse displays, a different job).
    -->
    <Script><![CDATA[
        -- ref TaxiFrame.lua:2-3, verbatim.
        TAXI_MAP_WIDTH = 316
        TAXI_MAP_HEIGHT = 352

        -- The static node-button pool's size — see deviation 1 above.
        BENILLA_TAXI_MAX_NODES = 50

        -- ref TaxiFrame.lua:7-16, verbatim (the three icon states — CURRENT green / REACHABLE
        -- white / DISTANT yellow — all three files verified present in the MPQ this session).
        TaxiButtonTypes = { }
        TaxiButtonTypes["CURRENT"] = {
            file = "Interface\\TaxiFrame\\UI-Taxi-Icon-Green"
        }
        TaxiButtonTypes["REACHABLE"] = {
            file = "Interface\\TaxiFrame\\UI-Taxi-Icon-White"
        }
        TaxiButtonTypes["DISTANT"] = {
            file = "Interface\\TaxiFrame\\UI-Taxi-Icon-Yellow"
        }

        -- Byte-exact 1.12 enUS GlobalStrings (interface.MPQ `GlobalStrings.lua`, line-cited).
        -- `TEXT(x)` (ref l.121) is the real client's build-time no-op localization macro — every
        -- `TEXT(FOO)` call is transcribed as the bare `FOO` global (CharacterFrame.xml's own
        -- convention); with no engine `TEXT` global at all, these are plain locals instead.
        local TAXINODEYOUAREHERE = "You are here" -- GlobalStrings.lua:4232
        -- GlobalStrings.lua:1864 — the reference's own byte, including its curly apostrophe
        -- (U+2019, "don\226\128\153t"), not a straight one.
        local ERR_TAXINOPATHS = "You don\226\128\153t know any flight locations connected to this one."

        function TaxiFrame_OnLoad()
            local frame = this
            -- The "npc" portrait token (decision 0421): the open taxi session's flight master
            -- bakes into the ring, resolved exactly like Gossip/Merchant/Trainer's own OnLoad.
            SetPortraitTexture(getglobal(frame:GetName() .. "Portrait"), "npc")
            frame:RegisterEvent("TAXIMAP_OPENED")
            frame:RegisterEvent("TAXIMAP_CLOSED")
        end

        -- Deviation 2 above: the flight master's name rides TAXIMAP_OPENED's arg1 (the app
        -- resolves it through the NameCache) rather than a live UnitName("npc") read.
        function BenillaTaxiFrame_SetTitle(name)
            getglobal("TaxiNameText"):SetText(name or "")
        end

        -- ref TaxiFrame.lua:24-80, restructured only at the node-button loop (deviation 1 — a
        -- fixed pool walked 1..BENILLA_TAXI_MAX_NODES instead of grown via CreateFrame).
        function TaxiFrame_OnEvent(event)
            local frame = this
            if event == "TAXIMAP_OPENED" then
                BenillaTaxiFrame_SetTitle(arg1)

                -- Set the texture coords on the map, then hand the region to the app's art pick.
                TaxiMap:SetTexCoord(0, 1, 0, 1)
                SetTaxiMap(TaxiMap)

                -- Draw nodes: every pool slot up to the pushed count shows its type's icon at its
                -- pushed position; the rest hide (ref l.44-63, the static-pool shape).
                local num_nodes = NumTaxiNodes()
                for index = 1, BENILLA_TAXI_MAX_NODES do
                    local button = getglobal("TaxiButton" .. index)
                    local ntype = TaxiNodeGetType(index)
                    if index <= num_nodes and ntype ~= "NONE" then
                        local x, y = TaxiNodePosition(button:GetID())
                        button:ClearAllPoints()
                        button:SetPoint("CENTER", "TaxiMap", "BOTTOMLEFT", x * TAXI_MAP_WIDTH, y * TAXI_MAP_HEIGHT)
                        button:SetNormalTexture(TaxiButtonTypes[ntype].file)
                        button:Show()
                    else
                        button:Hide()
                    end
                end

                -- All set...
                ShowUIPanel(frame)
                if not frame:IsVisible() then
                    CloseTaxiMap()
                end
                return
            end
            if event == "TAXIMAP_CLOSED" then
                HideUIPanel(frame)
                return
            end
        end

        -- ref TaxiFrame.lua:82-126, verbatim. `this:GetID()` (l.96) reads the SAME button as the
        -- `button` parameter — the engine sets the shared `this` global to the invoking frame
        -- before OnEnter runs (decision 0068's event-dispatch convention), exactly like the real
        -- client, so the two reads agree.
        function TaxiNodeOnButtonEnter(button)
            local index = button:GetID()
            GameTooltip:SetOwner(button, "ANCHOR_RIGHT")
            GameTooltip:AddLine(TaxiNodeName(index), "", 1.0, 1.0, 1.0)

            -- Setup variables
            local numRoutes = GetNumRoutes(index)
            local line
            local sX, sY, dX, dY
            local w = TaxiRouteMap:GetWidth()
            local h = TaxiRouteMap:GetHeight()

            local ntype = TaxiNodeGetType(index)
            if ntype == "REACHABLE" then
                SetTooltipMoney(GameTooltip, TaxiNodeCost(this:GetID()))
                TaxiNodeSetCurrent(index)

                if numRoutes > NUM_TAXI_ROUTES then
                    for i = NUM_TAXI_ROUTES + 1, numRoutes do
                        line = TaxiRouteMap:CreateTexture("TaxiRoute" .. i, "BACKGROUND")
                        line:SetTexture("Interface\\TaxiFrame\\UI-Taxi-Line")
                    end
                    NUM_TAXI_ROUTES = numRoutes
                end

                for i = 1, NUM_TAXI_ROUTES do
                    line = getglobal("TaxiRoute" .. i)
                    if i <= numRoutes then
                        sX = TaxiGetSrcX(index, i) * w
                        sY = TaxiGetSrcY(index, i) * h
                        dX = TaxiGetDestX(index, i) * w
                        dY = TaxiGetDestY(index, i) * h
                        DrawRouteLine(line, "TaxiRouteMap", sX, sY, dX, dY, 32)
                        line:Show()
                    else
                        line:Hide()
                    end
                end
            elseif ntype == "CURRENT" then
                GameTooltip:AddLine(TAXINODEYOUAREHERE, "", 0.5, 1.0, 0.5)
                DrawOneHopLines()
            end

            GameTooltip:Show()
        end

        NUM_TAXI_ROUTES = 0

        -- Draw all flightpaths within one hop of current location — ref TaxiFrame.lua:129-165,
        -- verbatim except the canvas name ("TaxiRouteMap" -> "TaxiRouteMap").
        function DrawOneHopLines()
            local line
            local sX, sY, dX, dY
            local w = TaxiRouteMap:GetWidth()
            local h = TaxiRouteMap:GetHeight()
            local numNodes = NumTaxiNodes()
            local numLines = 0
            local numSingleHops = 0
            for i = 1, numNodes do
                if GetNumRoutes(i) == 1 then
                    numSingleHops = numSingleHops + 1
                    numLines = numLines + 1
                    if numLines > NUM_TAXI_ROUTES then
                        line = TaxiRouteMap:CreateTexture("TaxiRoute" .. numLines, "BACKGROUND")
                        line:SetTexture("Interface\\TaxiFrame\\UI-Taxi-Line")
                        NUM_TAXI_ROUTES = numLines
                    else
                        line = getglobal("TaxiRoute" .. numLines)
                    end
                    if line then
                        sX = TaxiGetSrcX(i, 1) * w
                        sY = TaxiGetSrcY(i, 1) * h
                        dX = TaxiGetDestX(i, 1) * w
                        dY = TaxiGetDestY(i, 1) * h
                        DrawRouteLine(line, "TaxiRouteMap", sX, sY, dX, dY, 32)
                        line:Show()
                    end
                end
            end
            for i = numLines + 1, NUM_TAXI_ROUTES do
                getglobal("TaxiRoute" .. i):Hide()
            end
            if numSingleHops == 0 then
                UIErrorsFrame:AddMessage(ERR_TAXINOPATHS, 1.0, 0.1, 0.1)
                HideUIPanel(TaxiFrame)
            end
        end


        -- The following function is used with permission from Daniel Stephens
        -- <iriel@vigilance-committee.org> — ref TaxiFrame.lua:168-226, byte-for-byte verbatim (pure
        -- Lua line-quad math over the engine's 8-arg affine SetTexCoord; no engine dependency beyond
        -- what the phase-1 seam test already proved: CreateTexture, SetTexCoord's 8-arg form,
        -- SetPoint with a string canvas name).
        TAXIROUTE_LINEFACTOR = 32/30 -- Multiplying factor for texture coordinates
        TAXIROUTE_LINEFACTOR_2 = TAXIROUTE_LINEFACTOR / 2 -- Half o that

        -- T        - Texture
        -- C        - Canvas Frame (for anchoring)
        -- sx,sy    - Coordinate of start of line
        -- ex,ey    - Coordinate of end of line
        -- w        - Width of line
        -- relPoint - Relative point on canvas to interpret coords (Default BOTTOMLEFT)
        function DrawRouteLine(T, C, sx, sy, ex, ey, w, relPoint)
           if (not relPoint) then relPoint = "BOTTOMLEFT"; end

           -- Determine dimensions and center point of line
           local dx,dy = ex - sx, ey - sy;
           local cx,cy = (sx + ex) / 2, (sy + ey) / 2;

           -- Normalize direction if necessary
           if (dx < 0) then
              dx,dy = -dx,-dy;
           end

           -- Calculate actual length of line
           local l = sqrt((dx * dx) + (dy * dy));

           -- Quick escape if it's zero length
           if (l == 0) then
              T:SetTexCoord(0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0);
              T:SetPoint("BOTTOMLEFT", C, relPoint, cx,cy);
              T:SetPoint("TOPRIGHT",   C, relPoint, cx,cy);
              return;
           end

           -- Sin and Cosine of rotation, and combination (for later)
           local s,c = -dy / l, dx / l;
           local sc = s * c;

           -- Calculate bounding box size and texture coordinates
           local Bwid, Bhgt, BLx, BLy, TLx, TLy, TRx, TRy, BRx, BRy;
           if (dy >= 0) then
              Bwid = ((l * c) - (w * s)) * TAXIROUTE_LINEFACTOR_2;
              Bhgt = ((w * c) - (l * s)) * TAXIROUTE_LINEFACTOR_2;
              BLx, BLy, BRy = (w / l) * sc, s * s, (l / w) * sc;
              BRx, TLx, TLy, TRx = 1 - BLy, BLy, 1 - BRy, 1 - BLx;
              TRy = BRx;
           else
              Bwid = ((l * c) + (w * s)) * TAXIROUTE_LINEFACTOR_2;
              Bhgt = ((w * c) + (l * s)) * TAXIROUTE_LINEFACTOR_2;
              BLx, BLy, BRx = s * s, -(l / w) * sc, 1 + (w / l) * sc;
              BRy, TLx, TLy, TRy = BLx, 1 - BRx, 1 - BLx, 1 - BLy;
              TRx = TLy;
           end

           -- Set texture coordinates and anchors
           T:ClearAllPoints();
           T:SetTexCoord(TLx, TLy, BLx, BLy, TRx, TRy, BRx, BRy);
           T:SetPoint("BOTTOMLEFT", C, relPoint, cx - Bwid, cy - Bhgt);
           T:SetPoint("TOPRIGHT",   C, relPoint, cx + Bwid, cy + Bhgt);
        end

        function BenillaTaxiCloseButton_OnClick()
            -- vanilla's client-side close sends no packet; the app clears TaxiState on this
            -- intent (which fires TAXIMAP_CLOSED), and we hide immediately so there's no lag.
            CloseTaxiMap()
            HideUIPanel(TaxiFrame)
        end
    ]]></Script>

    <!--
        The node-button pool's virtual template (ref TaxiButtonTemplate, l.4-32): a 16×16 button,
        the type icon assigned per repaint via SetNormalTexture (deviation 1's static pool — see
        the header note), the 32×32 CENTER highlight glow. OnEnter/OnLeave/OnClick are the ref's,
        byte for byte (l.12-20) — including the click firing UNCONDITIONALLY regardless of node
        type, exactly like the reference (a DISTANT/CURRENT click still queues TakeTaxiNode; the
        app-side drain treats a routeless click as a no-op — there is no RE'd finding for what the
        real client's native TakeTaxiNode does with an unreachable index, so this is the safe,
        undocumented-but-reasonable inference, not an asserted fact).
    -->
    <Button name="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" hidden="true" virtual="true">
        <Size>
            <AbsDimension x="16" y="16"/>
        </Size>
        <Anchors>
            <Anchor point="BOTTOMRIGHT"/>
        </Anchors>
        <Scripts>
            <OnEnter>
                TaxiNodeOnButtonEnter(this);
            </OnEnter>
            <OnLeave>
                GameTooltip:Hide();
            </OnLeave>
            <OnClick>
                TakeTaxiNode(this:GetID());
            </OnClick>
        </Scripts>
        <HighlightTexture file="Interface\TaxiFrame\UI-Taxi-Icon-Highlight">
            <Size x="32" y="32"/>
            <Anchors>
                <Anchor point="CENTER">
                    <Offset>
                        <AbsDimension x="0" y="0"/>
                    </Offset>
                </Anchor>
            </Anchors>
        </HighlightTexture>
    </Button>

    <Frame name="TaxiFrame" hidden="true">
        <!-- The real 384×512 window (ref l.34-36). No <Anchors> — ShowUIPanel/SetLeftFrame
             SetPoints this to the left slot on open, exactly like Gossip/Merchant/Trainer. -->
        <Size><AbsDimension x="384" y="512"/></Size>
        <Layers>
            <!-- NPC portrait 58×58 TOPLEFT (8,-9) (ref TaxiPortrait, l.46-57), BACKGROUND —
                 drawn under the ARTWORK quadrant slabs below so their frame art rings it. -->
            <Layer level="BACKGROUND">
                <Texture name="$parentPortrait">
                    <Size><AbsDimension x="58" y="58"/></Size>
                    <Anchors>
                        <Anchor point="TOPLEFT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="8" y="-9"/></Offset></Anchor>
                    </Anchors>
                </Texture>
            </Layer>
            <!-- The four TaxiFrame quadrant slabs that ARE the window art (ref l.59-103): 256-wide
                 left halves, 128-wide right halves, each 256 tall, pinned to their corner. No
                 <TexCoords> — each samples its whole texture. -->
            <Layer level="ARTWORK">
                <Texture file="Interface\TaxiFrame\UI-TaxiFrame-TopLeft">
                    <Size><AbsDimension x="256" y="256"/></Size>
                    <Anchors><Anchor point="TOPLEFT"/></Anchors>
                </Texture>
                <Texture file="Interface\TaxiFrame\UI-TaxiFrame-TopRight">
                    <Size><AbsDimension x="128" y="256"/></Size>
                    <Anchors><Anchor point="TOPLEFT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="256" y="0"/></Offset></Anchor></Anchors>
                </Texture>
                <Texture file="Interface\TaxiFrame\UI-TaxiFrame-BotLeft">
                    <Size><AbsDimension x="256" y="256"/></Size>
                    <Anchors><Anchor point="TOPLEFT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="0" y="-256"/></Offset></Anchor></Anchors>
                </Texture>
                <Texture file="Interface\TaxiFrame\UI-TaxiFrame-BotRight">
                    <Size><AbsDimension x="128" y="256"/></Size>
                    <Anchors><Anchor point="TOPLEFT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="256" y="-256"/></Offset></Anchor></Anchors>
                </Texture>
                <!-- The flight master's name banner (ref TaxiMerchant, l.104-115): GameFontNormal,
                     CENTER, TOP -17, 192 wide — deviation 2 above (arg1, not UnitName("npc")). -->
                <FontString name="TaxiNameText" inherits="GameFontNormal" justifyH="CENTER">
                    <Size><AbsDimension x="192" y="0"/></Size>
                    <Anchors>
                        <Anchor point="TOP"><Offset><AbsDimension x="0" y="-17"/></Offset></Anchor>
                    </Anchors>
                </FontString>
            </Layer>
            <!-- The continent map art (ref TaxiMap, l.117-129): 316×352, TOP -13,-75. No file —
                 SetTaxiMap assigns the app's TAXIMAP<continentId> pick (byte-verified — decision 0496). -->
            <Layer level="OVERLAY">
                <Texture name="TaxiMap">
                    <Size><AbsDimension x="316" y="352"/></Size>
                    <Anchors>
                        <Anchor point="TOP"><Offset><AbsDimension x="-13" y="-75"/></Offset></Anchor>
                    </Anchors>
                </Texture>
            </Layer>
        </Layers>
        <Frames>
            <!-- Close: the real UIPanelCloseButton position (TOPRIGHT -29,-8; ref l.133-141), on
                 the minimize-button art (this engine ships no UIPanelCloseButton — the Gossip/
                 Trainer/Merchant precedent). -->
            <Button name="TaxiCloseButton">
                <Size><AbsDimension x="32" y="32"/></Size>
                <Anchors>
                    <Anchor point="TOPRIGHT"><Offset><AbsDimension x="-29" y="-8"/></Offset></Anchor>
                </Anchors>
                <NormalTexture file="Interface\Buttons\UI-Panel-MinimizeButton-Up"/>
                <PushedTexture file="Interface\Buttons\UI-Panel-MinimizeButton-Down"/>
                <HighlightTexture file="Interface\Buttons\UI-Panel-MinimizeButton-Highlight" alphaMode="ADD"/>
                <Scripts><OnClick>BenillaTaxiCloseButton_OnClick()</OnClick></Scripts>
            </Button>

            <!-- `<TaxiRouteFrame>` (ref l.142-153) — an intrinsic type this engine doesn't have —
                 becomes a plain <Frame> (see the header note): 316×352, TOP -13,-75, exactly
                 overlaid on TaxiMap. Houses the node-button pool + the dynamically-created
                 route-line textures, both parented here exactly like the reference (ref l.39,101). -->
            <Frame name="TaxiRouteMap">
                <Size><AbsDimension x="316" y="352"/></Size>
                <Anchors>
                    <Anchor point="TOP"><Offset><AbsDimension x="-13" y="-75"/></Offset></Anchor>
                </Anchors>
                <Frames>
                <Button name="TaxiButton1" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="1"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton2" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="2"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton3" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="3"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton4" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="4"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton5" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="5"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton6" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="6"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton7" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="7"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton8" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="8"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton9" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="9"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton10" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="10"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton11" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="11"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton12" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="12"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton13" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="13"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton14" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="14"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton15" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="15"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton16" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="16"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton17" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="17"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton18" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="18"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton19" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="19"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton20" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="20"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton21" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="21"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton22" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="22"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton23" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="23"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton24" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="24"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton25" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="25"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton26" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="26"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton27" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="27"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton28" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="28"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton29" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="29"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton30" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="30"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton31" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="31"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton32" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="32"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton33" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="33"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton34" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="34"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton35" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="35"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton36" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="36"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton37" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="37"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton38" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="38"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton39" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="39"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton40" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="40"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton41" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="41"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton42" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="42"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton43" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="43"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton44" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="44"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton45" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="45"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton46" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="46"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton47" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="47"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton48" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="48"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton49" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="49"/>
                <Button name="TaxiButton50" inherits="BenillaTaxiButtonTemplate" id="50"/>
                </Frames>
            </Frame>
        </Frames>
        <Scripts>
            <OnLoad>
                TaxiFrame_OnLoad()
            </OnLoad>
            <OnEvent>
                TaxiFrame_OnEvent(event)
            </OnEvent>
            <!-- ref l.162-169, verbatim: the MainMenu sound kit (not Merchant/Trainer's
                 CharacterInfo kit — the reference genuinely uses a different pair here). -->
            <OnShow>
                PlaySound("igMainMenuOpen");
                DrawOneHopLines();
            </OnShow>
            <OnHide>
                CloseTaxiMap();
                PlaySound("igMainMenuClose")
            </OnHide>
        </Scripts>
    </Frame>
</Ui>
